  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Pinpointing the Root Issue**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core of the image and map inconsistencies during deployment. The issue stems from the `DeployScreen.tsx` file, specifically lines 281-285. My investigation points to the `getMapImage(mapId)` function as the culprit. I am still investigating.\n\n\n**Addressing the Map Display**\n\nI\'ve determined that `DeployScreen.tsx` lacks tile rendering, leading to issues with maps constructed from tilesets or dynamic paths. My solution now includes updating `DeployScreen.tsx` to use the official map image path or `getMapImage` and, critically, integrate the tile rendering canvas like `BattleCanvas2D.tsx`. This guarantees identical map display across Deploy and Battle screens, handling custom maps and API-registered maps correctly.\n\n\n"
